meta {
  name: Delete Webhook
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/webhooks/{{webhookId}}
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: inherit
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  "{}":
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false
}

docs {
  Permanently removes a webhook — the Delete a Webhook endpoint. This is a destructive,
  irreversible operation: once deleted, that webhook subscription is gone and must be recreated
  from scratch (with a new ID) if you want it back.

  **Parameters**
  - `webhookId` (path) — the ID of the webhook to delete. Bound to the collection variable
    `{{webhookId}}`, populated with an example ID — replace it with the ID of the webhook you
    actually want to remove (from "List Webhooks").

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/webhooks/delete-a-webhook

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
